WEBVTT

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.780
Kurume, Kyushu.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.870
We've come a long way.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.870
I never dreamed I'd get to travel with you 
over summer vacation, Koizumi-san.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.380
You just followed me uninvited.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:34.300
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:34.300
<b>Chiba</b>

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:34.300
<b>Toyama</b>

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.870
From Tokyo, we went to Chiba.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.600
The we went north to Aomori.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.300
<b>Aomori</b>

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.300
<b>Hakata 
Saga 
Kumamoto</b>

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.300
We traveled along the coast of the 
Sea of Japan, and now we're in Kyushu.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.940
It'll go cold if you don't hurry up and eat.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.520
Okay.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.990
Hey, Koizumi-san, where are we going next?

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.440
This can't be the end, right?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.750
Of course it's not.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.050
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:12.960
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.640
Summer vacation starts tomorrow.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.000
<b>Nationwide</b>

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.620
I hope that all of you, whether you
plan to attend college or not,

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.810
spend your summer vacation 
in a meaningful way.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.500
Class representative, if you would.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.630
Stand!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.140
It's over!

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.900
Talk about liberation!

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.390
Summer break is finally here!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.400
Where should we go?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.900
A meaningful summer vacation, huh?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.060
Wanna kick it off with a trip somewhere?

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:54.910
I'm in!

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.720
Okinawa? Daimon?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.800
Bali!

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.390
This is gonna be the best!

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.930
How are you going to pay for that?

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.400
We'll work it out somehow.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.540
That's right!

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.760
I have cram school, so I won't 
have much time to hang out.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.290
What's more important? 
College or your friends?

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:10.410
College.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.580
You're absolutely right.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.720
Hey, Koizumi-san!

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.670
What are you doing over summer vacation?

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.100
Want to go on a trip with us?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:21.530
Please?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:21.840
Please?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.750
Hold on, Yuu!

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.860
I'll pass.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.210
What?!

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.530
But we could go to Okinawa, 
or Taiwan, or Bali,

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.270
and have all kinds of 
unusual ramen together!

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.200
Hey, for starters, why don't 
we hang out tomorrow?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.230
No, thank you.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.430
I'm going on a trip tomorrow.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.560
Where to?

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.550
The entire nation of Japan.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.550
The entire nation?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.540
Hey, Yuu!

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.550
I'm finally here.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.880
Good morning.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.790
You're both late!

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.550
But we're right on time!

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.470
You have to get in line before they open!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.140
It's summer break, so let's 
get our heads in the game!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.310
She's so excited.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.810
Three adults, separate!

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.070
Here we go!

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.890
You gotta start with this one!

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.040
You think so?

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.260
Take the picture, Yuu!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.130
Okay.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.430
The wild beast of Asakusa,
finally tamed!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.240
Hey, I got a "like."

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.070
Misa looks like she's having a good time.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.260
I'm glad.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.310
Not yesterday...

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.880
Why are we going to Asakusa the first day?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.230
I'd rather go to Land or Sea!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.540
Sorry, but I have cram school in the evening.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.450
And it's my turn to make dinner tonight.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.430
That's why we decided to go 
to the nearest amusement park.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.370
Which is easier on our wallets, too.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.120
Let's do that one next! That one!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.630
<b>Haunted House
Famous</b>

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.530
Let's go in the haunted house.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.880
Roger!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.210
Aren't we too old for a haunted house?

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.120
Jeez, those two...

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.110
That was pretty legit.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.770
It was fun.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.090
I thought I heard a cute little scream, too...

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.150
Don't remind me.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.200
Let's go on that one next!

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.580
Okay!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.660
Can we take a break first?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.660
That was really fun.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.080
So you had fun after all.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.540
I guess.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.700
Wow, yukata.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.630
Is there some kind of festival today?

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.710
It's probably from there.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.050
<b>Yukata Rental</b>

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.220
<b>Asakusa Transformations</b>

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.720
<b>Asakusa Transformations</b>

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.010
A rental shop, huh?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.720
Looks fun!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.070
This is great.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:18.480
Which one do I want?

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.480
Ta-da!

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.110
That looks great!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.620
Y-You really think so?

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:35.990
It's so crowded.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.400
It <i>is</i> the first day of summer break.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.640
I love when things are busy like this!

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.380
It really gets me hyped!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.200
Not me.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.640
What is it, Yuu?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.880
I think I saw Koizumi-san.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.640
Are you starting to go nuts or what?

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:56.680
All right!

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.200
Take it, take it!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:58.850
Yay!

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.520
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.030
<b>Nakamise</b>

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.790
<b>Jumbo Melon Buns</b>

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.790
<b>Getsunichido</b>

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.260
I found the melon buns!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.790
That's quite a long line.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.540
<b>Since 1945</b>

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:20.540
It looks great!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.720
<b>Nishi-Sando</b>

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.720
<b>Asakusa
Shrine</b>

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.840
How about a little break?

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:34.640
Agreed.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.720
Let's do it.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.870
Here you go.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.480
That's so pretty!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.970
Just looking at it cools me down.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.560
Let's eat!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.860
Hey, didn't we have to do a report 
as part of our summer homework?

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.950
Oh, you mean that thing where 
we talk about our future?

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.280
We had an assignment like that?

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.510
You didn't even check the homework?

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.560
What are you guys going to write?

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.420
Is there something you can see 
yourselves doing in the future?

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.490
The future, huh?

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.270
Hmm... I don't know.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.760
I haven't given it any serious thought yet.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.430
I haven't even decided if 
I want to study further.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.510
You don't want to go to college?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:21.650
Well, if I become a pop idol or a model, 
I won't have time for school.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:24.230
Uh, yeah. You're right.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.090
But you're going to college, right, Jun?

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.480
What kind of schools are you thinking of?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.070
Well, I'm actually not even close to deciding.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.640
Just go with whatever.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.830
I mean, entrance exams 
are way in the future.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.820
Yup, yup.

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:43.590
I envy you two for being able 
to give this so little thought.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.480
I feel like we just got dissed.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.090
So Yuu, what are you going to do?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:53.200
I guess something to do with ramen.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:55.590
What? You, and not Koizumi?

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:59.050
I'll be doing it with her, of course.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.890
Doing what with her, exactly?

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.380
I will...

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:09.020
Yes, I will bring Koizumi-san,
who loves ramen, to the entire world!

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.020
<b>Koizumi</b>

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.020
<b>Koizumi-san's
100 Secrets</b>

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.020
<b>Spotlight on 
the young 
beauty of 
the new 
generation!</b>

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.100
Through magazines, videos, and concerts!

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.520
I feel stupid for asking 
you a serious question.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.860
You're embarrassing me. Please stop.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.450
What should we have for lunch?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.150
You've been talking about 
Koizumi-san all this time.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.920
Now we can't think of anything but ramen.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.920
<b>Yoroiya Ramen</b>

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.460
Here you go.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.050
Time to eat!

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.900
So good!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.850
There's something about eating 
hot ramen on a hot day.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.900
The other day, you said you didn't like that.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:59.160
But once in a while, you just get a 
craving for this chuuka soba flavor.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:02.160
My umeshio is really good, too.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.130
Thank you!

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.790
That was great.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.390
Next time, let's invite Koizumi-san, too.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:12.880
She might even be here now.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.930
Nah, no way.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.150
She said she was going on a trip today.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.550
<b>Recycled Kimono</b>

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.550
<b>Asakusa Transformations</b>

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.550
We really enjoyed ourselves after all, huh?

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.450
Because I got our spirits up.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.150
I guess I'll be going, then. 
It's almost time for cram school.

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.990
I'm going home this way, too.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.730
Okay. Well, I'm going this way.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:32.770
See you!

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:33.370
Later.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.570
Bye!

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.280
I want to come here again sometime.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:46.120
Hopefully, next time,
it'll be with Koizumi-san.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.880
Look at this, Koizumi-san.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.830
These chopsticks look 
perfect for eating ramen.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:53.420
Oh!

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.740
Yuu-san, these look so good.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.120
You're right.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.030
It's beautiful.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.450
It's like the starry sky fell to Earth.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:05.500
You're quite the romantic, aren't you?

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.010
All right!

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:13.000
Sometime during summer break,
I'm going to invite Koizumi-san here!

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.580
I'll pass.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.690
K-Koizumi-san?!

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.630
What are you doing here?

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.950
How am I supposed to answer that?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.760
You said you were going on a trip today!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.160
I did. So I'll be leaving now.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.670
Wait, wait! Look!

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.830
<b>Yoroiya Ramen</b>

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.830
Did you know that place has some 
amazing soy sauce ramen?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.320
Of course I did.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.240
It's surprising to find ramen in Asakusa.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.400
Surprising?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.340
What are you talking about?

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:51.480
Asakusa... is the place where it all began.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.650
Where it all... began?

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:59.480
Hey, what do you have in that bag?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:02.120
Ramen I'm giving as gifts,
a copy of <i>Ramen Walker</i>,

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.940
and some ramen for when I get hungry.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.990
I wish I was ramen.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:18.860
Asakusa is the place where it all 
began? What does that mean?

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:25.720
Various stories exist, but more than 
100 years ago, during the Meiji Era,

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.090
a humble Chinese-style restaurant 
called Rairaiken that originated

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.040
here in Asakusa made this soy sauce ramen.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:38.270
They say that's the origin of Japanese ramen 
with char siu and bamboo shoots.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.710
More than 100 years ago?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:54.540
<b>Yoroiya Ramen</b>

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.390
The person who owns this restaurant 
was born and raised in Asakusa.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:49.920
Honoring the history of Asakusa,
the birthplace of ramen,

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.340
he continues to maintain 
the old nostalgic taste.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.540
I didn't know that.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.440
So that's why the ramen 
tasted kind of nostalgic.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:01.520
You know, this is the first time 
I've seen you in your regular clothes.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.120
Anyway, I have to go now.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.270
Wait, where are you going on your trip?

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:08.220
Where?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:08.970
Yeah!

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.440
I'm already on it.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.480
Koizumi-san! Take me with you!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.980
<b>Jikaseimen
Ito</b>

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.030
This place looks quaint.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:24.320
<b>Jikaseimen Ito</b>

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.120
I'm going in.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.940
Hey, wait!

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.560
This is a pretty simple ramen.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:30.040
These are Kujuukuri's deluxe dried sardines.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:36.830
Each bowl contains a generous 40 grams of
sardines, making the soup rich in umami.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:39.200
Another soy sauce ramen place, huh?

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.290
Time to eat.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.470
Delicious!

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.860
<i>It seems simple, but the flavor has depth.</i>

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.360
<i>That was so good!</i>

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.610
<b>Aomori Niboshi Chuuka Soba</b>

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.620
This is next.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.610
Oh, Aomori ramen?

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:09.750
They specialize in dried sardines, too?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.570
Yes.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.700
This looks so good!

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.830
The scent of the soy sauce 
and dashi is amazing.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:21.570
Aomori ramen, which has its origins in 
soba, is known for using no fat at all.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:24.210
You're right! I don't see any fat at all.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.190
It does have a really light taste.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.640
And that brings out the taste of the sardines.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.240
That was so good.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.500
It's almost time.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.080
<b>Yoroiya Ramen</b>

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.080
Wait, isn't this place...

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.690
I ate here earlier today with Misa and Jun.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.840
Then you don't need to line up.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:07.230
Ramen I eat with you goes 
into another stomach!

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.340
What is this? The soup is black!

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:15.890
When I was here before,
they didn't have anything like this.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.860
This is limited to their evening menu.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:18.810
Limited?

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:21.390
This is ramen from Toyama 
in the Hokuriku region,

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:22.960
called Toyama Black.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.800
This restaurant serves their own take on it.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.660
I'm going to eat, too.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:44.750
Such a bold flavor!

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:47.500
I really like the black pepper and yuzu accents.

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:56.220
So we've been to Aomori, 
and now we're in Toyama.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.520
It really feels like we're on a trip.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.900
Which is why I said that in the first place.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:14.410
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:14.410
<b>Toyama</b>

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:04.690
The soy sauce ramen born in Tokyo's Shitamachi

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:07.920
made its way all over the country, 
undergoing all sorts of evolutions.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:14.110
You can encounter ramen from all over Japan 
just by walking around here in Asakusa.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.410
<b>Aomori</b>

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:20.500
I'm on a trip to experience that right now.

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:21.860
I see.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:24.660
You really were on a trip, huh?

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.380
I said so, right from the start.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.830
I get it.

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:32.300
I'm on a trip with you right now.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.570
Well, I'm still on my trip, so...

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.010
Wait, wait!

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.980
Since I've come this far, 
I'll stick with you to the end.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.100
Please!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.410
Do as you like.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.190
I will!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.480
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.320
<b>Hakata Ramen</b>

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.320
Look, it's tonkotsu!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.280
My favorite!

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.350
Time to eat!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.080
Yum!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:07.110
People simply call it "Hakata ramen," 
but it has many different variations.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:12.930
This store's specialty is rich tonkotsu soup
from tonkotsu's birthplace, Kurume,

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.200
and these straight, thin noodles.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:22.680
<b>Aomori</b>

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.900
Kurume, Kyushu.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:23.850
<b>Toyama</b>

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:23.850
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:23.850
<b>Chiba</b>

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.980
We've come a long way.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.850
<b>Hakata 
Saga 
Kumamoto</b>

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:30.360
<b>Saga Ramen</b>

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:27.290
And this legendary restaurant, Saga Ramen,

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:31.130
has inherited the flavor of the famous 
restaurant in Saga, Seiyouken.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:34.780
Their specialty is a thick tonkotsu soup 
that has simmered for months,

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.860
paired with soft, thick noodles.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.860
You're right! These noodles are kind of thick.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:47.310
The noodles are so soft.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:50.630
There's a lot of variety in tonkotsu ramen, too.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.410
Ah, thank you for that meal!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.880
<b>Benkei</b>

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.880
<b>Ramen</b>

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.880
<b>Asakusa Main Branch</b>

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:56.880
This is the last restaurant for today.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:00.150
You don't have to overextend 
yourself to go with me.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.760
I've come this far! I won't leave now!

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.850
Is this a soy sauce tonkotsu?

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.400
This is Eddoko ramen, 
much loved in the Shitamachi district.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:12.600
This is the flavor that spread 
out from here in Asakusa.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.650
It looks so rich!

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:16.860
Time to eat!

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:28.050
<i>The ramen that was created in Asakusa
became tonkotsu in Kyushu, and now...</i>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<b>Aomori</b>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<b>Toyama</b>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<b>Chiba</b>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<b>Hakata
Saga
Kumamoto</b>

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.900
<i>...it's come back to Tokyo in this form.</i>

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:48.300
I think I ate enough ramen 
for my entire break.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.270
Didn't I warn you?

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.990
Yeah, you did.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:00.860
I just remembered the first time 
you and I had ramen together.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.160
I ate too much that day, too.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.220
When was that?

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:09.070
You don't remember?

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.050
No.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:11.160
Aw...

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:14.890
But anyway, even if we can't do it for real,

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:18.420
we can always go on a trip 
like this, through ramen.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.660
Actually, we should go 
on a real trip next time!

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.190
Like to Okinawa!

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:26.130
I'd love to see you in a bathing suit.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:26.980
No.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.160
Stingy...

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:30.190
I'm going now.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.020
Wait...

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.820
<b>Suzumi Fireworks Display</b>

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.130
Fireworks...

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.720
Look, Koizumi-san.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.600
<b>Suzumi Fireworks Display</b>

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:08.610
They're doing a fireworks display next week.

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.080
Let's go together!

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.100
I'll pass.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.020
What?! Let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.400
I want to see you in a yukata! 
Please, please, please...

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.400
No, thank you.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:20.120
Please! Pretty please!

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.220
No.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:30.290
<b>Grooowl</b>

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:31.090
Why'd you flake out when it was
your turn to make dinner?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:35.040
<b>Grooowl</b>

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:35.040
<b>Grooowl</b>

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:33.220
I was on a trip around the country.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:35.100
Oh, yeah?!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.050
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Local Instant Noodles</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Iekei</b>

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:15.430
Woo-hoo, I went on a trip around 
the country with Koizumi-san!

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:18.040
She's so cute when she's on a trip.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:21.620
Enough about your dreams.
Anyway, want to go to the beach with me?

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:22.870
Yeah, let's go!

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:24.450
We'll invite Koizumi-san, too.

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:27.600
Koizumi-san in a swimsuit...
Koizumi-san in a swimsuit...

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:29.460
She's never, ever gonna come.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:40.450
<b>Thank you for the food!</b>
